# Autonomous Research Loop — {{CAMPAIGN_TITLE}}

The **slim core** of the {{CAMPAIGN_KIND}} campaign protocol — what the agent re-reads **every
iteration**. Rarely-fired procedures live in `docs/protocols/`. **Run continuously until manually
stopped.**

> This loop folds scientific-rigor best practices directly into each iteration: a-priori bounding of
> expectations, uncertainty/error-type tracking, independent verification of every promotion, model
> parsimony and tie-breaking, simulation-gap caution, and full provenance logging.
> Items tagged **[PROPOSED]** are machine-suggested additions awaiting your review — keep or cut each.
> Everything untagged is settled campaign doctrine.

## Operating stance (applies to EVERY decision in the loop)
- **Critically evaluate every decision.** {{DECISION_EXAMPLES}} — each is a hypothesis, not a given.
  State why before you commit.
- **Assume you are wrong until independently proven right.** A number that converged, looks clean, or
  matches your hope is *suspect*, not *confirmed*. The burden of proof is on the positive result.
- **Prefer the minimally sufficient model/design.** Reach for the simplest {{MODEL_NOUNS}} that
  explains the data; add a parameter/term only when it earns its keep against the {{SPREAD_NOUN}}
  spread, is physically/theoretically motivated, AND generalizes. (Near-universal — apply by default.)
- **Use precise notation and units everywhere.** Name the quantity, its units, and its scale.
  {{UNITS_EXAMPLE_LINE}}. Ambiguous notation is how sign/convention bugs survive (see
  `docs/CONVENTIONS.md`).
- **Track uncertainty as a first-class output.** No bare point estimates — every metric you act on
  carries a spread (see Rigor). A result without an error bar is not yet a result.
- **Honesty is non-negotiable.** Report only numbers you actually computed from a real run — never
  estimate or fabricate. Truth matters more than a win: communicate openly even when results disappoint,
  keep every promise, and never fabricate a citation (full integrity doctrine: docs/PRINCIPLES.md).

