## The ONE metric (FROZEN — never edited mid-campaign)
`{{PRIMARY_METRIC}}` = {{METRIC_DEFINITION}}. {{PRIMARY_DIRECTION}} = better. Computed by
`{{FROZEN_SCORER_PATH}}` (FROZEN). **You change what FEEDS the metric, never how it is computed.**
- **Hard bounds:** {{METRIC_HARD_BOUNDS}}.
- **Plausible a-priori range:** {{METRIC_PLAUSIBLE_RANGE}} — predict before you run; a result OUTSIDE
  this range is a red flag to investigate, not a triumph.
- **Baseline (exp 000):** {{BASELINE_DESCRIPTION}} → the floor to beat. Measure it; don't assume it.
  Also keep the **trivial/degenerate reference** scores (all-zeros / constant / mean / a trivial physical
  state): a result that loses to a trivial answer is not a win, and a *non-physical* trivial answer that
  wins flags a metric/units error (protocols/baselines.md).
